<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, viewport-fit=cover">
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#0b0514">
    <title>Ghost / Superghost: a multiplayer word game</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Ghost (Superghost) is a multiplayer word game: add letters without completing a valid word too early. Open source, built with Swift and Vapor.">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/neon.css">
</head>

<body>
    <div id="site-nav"></div>

    <main class="page">
        <section class="hero gh-hero">
            <p class="sub-header">Game · Open Source</p>
            <h1>Spell carefully. Don't get <em>ghosted</em>.</h1>
            <p class="lead">Ghost (a.k.a. Superghost) is a multiplayer word game: players take turns adding letters without completing a valid word too early. Lose a round, gain a letter of G-H-O-S-T.</p>

            <div>
                <div class="tiles" id="tiles" aria-label="The letters G H O S T">
                    <span class="tile" style="--i:0">G</span>
                    <span class="tile" style="--i:1">H</span>
                    <span class="tile" style="--i:2">O</span>
                    <span class="tile" style="--i:3">S</span>
                    <span class="tile" style="--i:4">T</span>
                </div>
                <p class="tiles-hint">Click the tiles. Five losses and you are a ghost.</p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section>
            <div class="doc-content">
                <h2>How a round goes</h2>
                <p>The idea comes from a classroom game: one letter is added each turn, and the goal is to avoid completing a full word yourself. In this version players can <strong>prepend or append</strong>, which keeps rounds fast and a bit unpredictable.</p>
                <div class="round"><span class="who">You:</span><span class="word">S<span class="new">T</span></span><span class="who">: "st" is not a word. Safe.</span></div>
                <div class="round"><span class="who">Friend:</span><span class="word">ST<span class="new">A</span></span><span class="who">: "sta" is not a word either. Still safe.</span></div>
                <div class="round"><span class="who">You:</span><span class="word">STA<span class="new">R</span></span><span class="who">: "star" is a word. Game over.</span></div>
                <p>Multiplayer. Short rounds. Grudges included.</p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section>
            <div class="doc-content">
                <h2>Project details</h2>
                <p>Ghost is open source. The backend is written in Swift using Vapor. A small side game, not actively maintained. Code is public.</p>
                <div class="cta-buttons">
                    <a href="https://github.com/jinxd/superghost" class="nav-link">Source code</a>
                    <a href="/ghost/privacy" class="nav-link">Privacy</a>
                    <a href="/ghost/tos" class="nav-link">Terms</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>
    </main>

    <script src="/js/components.js"></script>
    <script>
        (function () {
            var tiles = document.querySelectorAll('#tiles .tile');
            if (!tiles.length) { return; }
            var ghosted = 0;
            tiles.forEach(function (tile) {
                tile.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
                    if (tile.classList.contains('ghosted')) {
                        tile.classList.remove('ghosted');
                        ghosted--;
                        return;
                    }
                    tile.classList.add('ghosted');
                    ghosted++;
                    if (ghosted === tiles.length && window.hnConfetti) {
                        window.hnConfetti(e.clientX, e.clientY, 80);
                    }
                });
            });
        })();
    </script>
</body>

</html>
